What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/120c0000.wifibt/verify_firmware
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Mollomm1 <68751598+Mollomm1@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Root-only write. Write a firmware name under postmarketos/mx140/
		(relative to the firmware search path) to check the image without
		staging or executing it. Uses direct filesystem firmware loading,
		without the userspace fallback. Checks magic, header/API version,
		lengths, entry-point bounds and header/constant/payload CRCs.
		Returns the loader or validation errno on failure. Paths containing
		".." are rejected. Normal use is:
		  echo postmarketos/mx140/mx140.bin > verify_firmware

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/120c0000.wifibt/firmware_status
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Mollomm1 <68751598+Mollomm1@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Returns "unchecked" before the first accepted check request.
		After a request, reports result (0 or negative errno), runtime
		length, entry point, and executed=0. A failed check clears the
		previous image metadata. Successful CRC checks do not establish
		firmware authenticity, board compatibility or runtime readiness.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/120c0000.wifibt/pmu_state
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Mollomm1 <68751598+Mollomm1@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Root-only read of six fixed always-on PMU registers: WiFi control
		nonsecure/secure (0x140/0x144), status (0x148), central sequencer
		status (0x384), and shared-memory size/base (0x7300/0x7304).
		Each line is "offset: value" in hexadecimal. Reads are sequential,
		not an atomic snapshot. No register writes, range dumps or mailbox
		accesses are performed. Nothing is sampled automatically in probe.
